itle":"color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWavyLine":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline","role":"symbol","title":"MXLWavyLine","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWavyLine","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Wavy lines are one way to indicate trills and vibrato. When used with a barline element, they should always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have type=“continue” set. The smufl attribute specifies a particular wavy line glyph from the SMuFL Multi-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment lines range.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWavyLine","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}